{
"dur": 46.428,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 8.32,
"text": "He was born in 1769 on Corsica, an island France had taken over just the year before. Napoleone di Buonaparte grew up speaking Italian.",
"end": 8.595
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.595,
"vo_start": 8.87,
"vo_end": 16.15,
"text": "At nine, he was sent to a military school in France. He had a thick accent and little money, and the other boys mocked him.",
"end": 16.425
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 16.425,
"vo_start": 16.7,
"vo_end": 24.5,
"text": "So he read. Maths, history, battles. He became an artillery officer at sixteen.",
"end": 24.775
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 24.775,
"vo_start": 25.05,
"vo_end": 33.77,
"text": "Then in 1789 the French Revolution broke the old order. Nobles fled or lost their heads. Suddenly, talent could matter more than birth.",
"end": 34.045
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 34.045,
"vo_start": 34.32,
"vo_end": 45.478,
"text": "In 1793, British and Spanish ships held the port of Toulon. Captain Bonaparte, aged twenty-four, saw where to put the cannons. His guns drove the ships from the harbour, and he was made a general.",
"end": 46.428
}
],
